<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec corn imports rise 1.69 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec corn imports rise 1.69 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's corn imports in December totalled 1,434,204 tonnes, up by 1.69 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data showed on Monday.</p>
<p>Total feed corn imports throughout calendar 1996 reached 11,453,034 tonnes against 11,681,998 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>Details were as follows, in tonnes:</p>
<p>			   Dec 96	  Nov 96	  Dec 95</p>
<p> Total		1,434,204     1,234,247     1,410,286</p>
<p> Feed corn total  1,034,537	 808,497     1,019,210</p>
<p> Others		 399,667	 425,750	 391,076</p>
<p>Top suppliers of feed corn (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		 1,015,844	 779,455	1,019,210</p>
<p> Argentina		5,000	  17,234		nil</p>
<p> South Africa	  13,693	  11,808		nil</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk (+81-3 3432-7391)</p>
</text>
